1. I named all the devices in the infrastructure according to their role in the network. 
  - The router is named Coffeeshop-Rtr and will provide access to the internet for the end devices. 
  - The Switch is Coffeeshop siwtch and will transfer data between devices. 
  - A PC and Printer are name were given MNGM names because they will be used be used to perform admin roles and have access to private data.
  - A PC and Printer were given the name POS becuase they will be handling and store customer confidential data. 
  - An Acces Point is named Coffeeshop-Ap because it will be providing wireless access to customers on a public guest network that is seperate from the private network. 

2. I connected all devices in the network using PoE cabling.
  - Router connected to ISP
  - Router Connedted to Switch
  - Switch connected MNGM-PC
  - Switch connected to MNGM-Printer
  - Switch connected to POS-Register
  - Switch connected to POS-Printer
  - Switch connected to Wireless-AP

3. Configuring the switch
  1. I gave the switch a hostname 
  2. Configure secret passcode
  3. Enabled password encryption
  4. Configured a "Message of the Day" banner
  5. Seperated the domain into multiple networks using vlan
    - VLAN 10: MANAGEMENT_OFFICE
    - VLAN 20: POS
    - VLAN 30: GUEST_WIFI
    - VLAN 99: NETWORK_MANAGEMENT ( Used ofr managing network devices)
  6. Congifure access mode on end devices and enable portfast
  7. Configure a trunk port for the router


